{"id": "EUVD-2026-32823", "enisaUuid": "fe32d4cf-1119-3716-9932-a7fcd570ac7a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntracepoint: balance regfunc() on func_add() failure in tracepoint_add_func()\n\nWhen a tracepoint goes through the 0 -> 1 transition, tracepoint_add_func()\ninvokes the subsystem's ext->regfunc() before attempting to install the\nnew probe via func_add(). If func_add() then fails (for example, when\nallocate_probes() cannot allocate a new probe array under memory pressure\nand returns -ENOMEM), the function returns the error without calling the\nmatching ext->unregfunc(), leaving the side effects of regfunc() behind\nwith no installed probe to justify them.\n\nFor syscall tracepoints this is particularly unpleasant: syscall_regfunc()\nbumps sys_tracepoint_refcount and sets SYSCALL_TRACEPOINT on every task.\nAfter a leaked failure, the refcount is stuck at a non-zero value with no\nconsumer, and every task continues paying the syscall trace entry/exit\noverhead until reboot. Other subsystems providing regfunc()/unregfunc()\npairs exhibit similarly scoped persistent state.\n\nMirror the existing 1 -> 0 cleanup and call ext->unregfunc() in the\nfunc_add() error path, gated on the same condition used there so the\nunwind is symmetric with the registration.", "datePublished": "2026-05-28T09:36:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T01:21:17", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5787052e5f69beb649f3d6a80a8aa37d9e683e4e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4f1756d043e56ea2e9a6c858fb290a0cf6fc2251", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/36ff362235307af95152d510b53c2d9b8773a342", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/247ed8a969f981bfba3112fd4bb441eaa6cef59c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7bcadb3c2bc1cf60690e931aadd35fb7bd646a49", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2c5b8eeea006eb694c81631cd5713d494b80be90", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/342829e042ac00f3d68d442ea92873fb6683f494", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fad217e16fded7f3c09f8637b0f6a224d58b5f2e"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-46196", "GHSA-3j98-4vrc-2fpm"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0352763a-ea8f-3c33-b2ef-caec0a2141f9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8cf868affdc459beee1a941df0cfaba1673740e3 <fad217e16fded7f3c09f8637b0f6a224d58b5f2e"}, {"id": "236299f2-aba9-3e11-9233-a9cb84725783", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8cf868affdc459beee1a941df0cfaba1673740e3 <4f1756d043e56ea2e9a6c858fb290a0cf6fc2251"}, {"id": "24bbb320-97db-391b-a542-5d14d43b5bc2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8cf868affdc459beee1a941df0cfaba1673740e3 <36ff362235307af95152d510b53c2d9b8773a342"}, {"id": "2f753f74-4bba-3ebd-88c2-1590b023e5e6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8cf868affdc459beee1a941df0cfaba1673740e3 <2c5b8eeea006eb694c81631cd5713d494b80be90"}, {"id": "494d7387-0c6c-3809-a567-f65e5aee4c12", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8cf868affdc459beee1a941df0cfaba1673740e3 <342829e042ac00f3d68d442ea92873fb6683f494"}, {"id": "49611cdf-fe09-3723-9a6c-05c3e7e82507", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.259"}, {"id": "4a3828da-cff0-309b-baa9-43e008e1a8d1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.210"}, {"id": "4a4af9d8-d2a1-38db-8f41-abe13dffeb74", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.88"}, {"id": "50d21aa4-0ff5-3a91-a392-e2201548cabb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.10"}, {"id": "58090e88-3792-3c14-a000-f2cfc04dd8b1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.7"}, {"id": "85ebd6b0-f3da-3b4e-91d4-eeb5059b50e5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.176"}, {"id": "9cc8f54e-640f-3151-8667-32995ae251e6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a3686e34-5b1b-3428-a76a-8c500d843807", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.30"}, {"id": "a953a8bc-c009-3703-bd99-384ccf68cf53", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8cf868affdc459beee1a941df0cfaba1673740e3 <7bcadb3c2bc1cf60690e931aadd35fb7bd646a49"}, {"id": "b12f3a0e-a080-39ac-ba0e-1b2906d19e19", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.140"}, {"id": "d108efe2-f6f6-3607-9624-cd340b260048", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8cf868affdc459beee1a941df0cfaba1673740e3 <5787052e5f69beb649f3d6a80a8aa37d9e683e4e"}, {"id": "f98093f3-0bd0-3395-bbcb-421f13cb50eb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8cf868affdc459beee1a941df0cfaba1673740e3 <247ed8a969f981bfba3112fd4bb441eaa6cef59c"}, {"id": "faffff1e-eb7b-37f9-887a-07ba240a4fe9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8aa649bd-ca24-38b6-8132-c39af8ec7b12", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}